+# architectureProducer
+
+The steps an architecture producer's stages call. `generate` and `validate` run the
+architecture-as-code tools in the `aac-tools` container, and `archive` archives the models
+AaC/Architecture collects. The steps carry what is the same in every producer: the container the
+tools run in, the tools' command lines, and an archive that the collector's filter matches. A
+value that differs per repo is an argument with no default: the stage and the producer id a deploy
+repo generates, and the model files a producer validates and archives.
+
+The pod declares the `aac-tools` container with [`podYaml`](podYaml.md)'s `aac-tools` template.
+Each step is a call on the var's method, so a declarative stage runs it in `script {}`. The file
+still writes out its every stage; the steps go inside them.
+
+```groovy
+agent {
+    kubernetes {
+        inheritFrom 'jenkins-agent'
+        yaml podYaml(templates: ['aac-tools'])
+    }
+}
+
+stages {
+    stage('Checkout') {
+        steps {
+            checkout scm
+        }
+    }
+
+    stage('Generate architecture') {
+        steps {
+            script {
+                architectureProducer.generate(stage: 'prd', producer: 'charts-deploy')
+                architectureProducer.archive(files: ['docs/architecture/*.yaml'])
+            }
+        }
+    }
+
+    stage('Validate architecture') {
+        steps {
+            script {
+                architectureProducer.validate(files: ['docs/architecture/*.yaml'])
+            }
+        }
+    }
+}
+```
+
+## Steps
+
+Every argument is required. A missing argument, an empty one or one the step does not take fails
+the build, and the error names it.
+
+### generate
+
+`architectureProducer.generate(stage: '<stage>', producer: '<id>')` runs
+`gen-architecture --stage <stage> --producer <id>` in the `aac-tools` container. gen-architecture
+renders the deploy repo's chart the way Argo CD renders that stage, reads the repo's judgment
+layer, `architecture.yaml` at the repo root, and writes `docs/architecture/<id>.yaml`.
+
+| Argument   | What it is                                                                          |
+| ---------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| `stage`    | The stage the file publishes: it names `config/<stage>/values.yaml`.                |
+| `producer` | The producer id, as Architecture's `pipeline-producers.yaml` registers it.          |
+
+### validate
+
+`architectureProducer.validate(files: [...])` runs `arch-validate` on the files in the `aac-tools`
+container. arch-validate submits each file to the architecture service, and a model the service
+rejects fails the build.
+
+| Argument | What it is                                                                                     |
+| -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| `files`  | A list of paths or shell globs, relative to the workspace, passed to `arch-validate` in order. |
+
+### archive
+
+`architectureProducer.archive(files: [...])` archives the files, fingerprinted, as the producer's
+artifact. AaC/Architecture copies from a producer's last successful build every `.yaml` file under
+a directory named `architecture`, at any depth, and nothing else. So each entry must be a pattern
+whose last segment ends in `.yaml`, under a path segment that is exactly `architecture`:
+`docs/architecture/*.yaml` passes, `*/architecture.yaml` fails the build before anything is
+archived. A pattern that matches no file fails the build too.
+
+| Argument | What it is                                                         |
+| -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |
+| `files`  | A list of Ant patterns, relative to the workspace.                 |
+
+The call goes in the stage that makes the artifact ([GRAN-3](../guide/stage-granularity.md#gran-3)):
+`Generate architecture` for a model the build generates, and the stage that validates it for a
+committed model.
+
+## Internals
+
+`generateCommand`, `validateCommand`, `archivePattern`, `paths`, `arguments` and `collected` check
